## Why This Is Asked
This question evaluates your ability to integrate external data stores with Kafka Streams while maintaining fault tolerance and delivery guarantees.

## Key Concepts
- TTL caches
- Side-input streams and cache invalidation
- MongoDB outage handling with exponential backoff strategy
- Offset management and at-least-once delivery guarantees
- Canary testing

## Code Example
```java
class EnrichmentSink {
  Map<String, VehicleRef> cache;

  void onEvent(VehicleEvent e) {
    VehicleRef ref = cache.get(e.vehicleId);
    if (ref == null) {
      ref = fetchFromMongoDB(e.vehicleId);
      cache.put(e.vehicleId, ref);
    }
    emit(enrich(e, ref));
  }

  void onRefUpdate(VehicleRef r) {
    cache.invalidate(r.vehicleId);
  }
}
```

## Why This Question Is Asked

This question evaluates real-world stateful Kafka Streams processing with a TTL-backed side-input, focusing on correctness under cache miss, update, and eviction scenarios, as well as robust testing strategies. It also assesses the ability to design APIs and observability for per-user enrichment in a high-throughput pipeline.

## Key Concepts

